 "structural_change": "S81-LINK5 L5B-LEPMU 10-21: s81sl_lepmu (475.2x691.2, lanes B on S, never closed) re-floorplanned to the lepw_mab_mu slot: 475.2 x 1900.8, pairs A+B on W in four lane bands [20,340] [640,960] [1020,1340] [1650,1880] (each inside its u_ln tile overlap), ro/ri/mu/clk on E, ml on N, fault S. MAIN-native: t5a lane-local TX columns (x 129.6) + per-lane RX SRAM column (x 388.8, 43.2 pitch, toward the E ri face) in the same lane band. REGATE after t5a/t5b native census FAIL (default params: max 1,559 loads, 694 drivers > 32; floorplan refused): kit params RX_SRAM 1 / IN_PIPE 1 / NATIVE32 1 = the Codex-qualified native32 structure of lep_mu_a/_h (6cb5f3eff, now plumbed through ot_s81sl_lep_mu_ab, defaults 0 unchanged); RX = 5 x 32x128 SRAM per lane. IN_PIPE adds +1 edge on ro / mu_c: die u_lep params + calendar are a LEAD call before bind. Clock: one TritonCTS tree, r6g recipe (no km16: r5e km16 lep twin 91.9/89.6). Same RTL as the die instance (e93685328) except the params listed, same ports and SDC.",
 "pin_regs": {
  "enable": false,
